{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And Shem took, and Yefet.</b> It is not written וַיִּקְחוּ but וַיִּקַּח — this teaches about Shem, that he exerted himself in the mitzvah more than Yefet. Therefore his sons merited the garment of tzitzit, and Yefet merited burial for his sons, as it says: ״I will give Gog a place there — a grave״ (Ezekiel 39). And Ham, who disgraced his father — concerning his seed it says: ״so the king of Assyria will lead the captives of Egypt and the exiles of Kush, boys and elders, barefoot and with buttocks exposed״ (Isaiah 20)." "<b>And their faces backward.</b> Why is it said a second time? This teaches that when they drew near to him and needed to turn themselves to cover him, they turned their faces backward."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:58:10.746139866Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}